&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT SPHINX&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sphinx builds software to solve complex national security problems in Space. Founded by engineers and technologists with deep experience across commercial and defense technology, we were frustrated by the outdated and insecure technology America&#39;s service members are forced to rely on. We&#39;re here to do better.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re focused on building modern, scalable products with an emphasis on using open source technologies. Expect talented, motivated, and interesting colleagues who emphasize collaboration, transparency, and individual responsibility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sphinx is hiring an &lt;strong&gt;Associate&amp;nbsp;DevOps Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join our team building a cutting edge communications platform for US government satellites. We&#39;re looking for a Junior DevOps Engineer to help take our build and deployment automation to the next level. As a Junior DevOps Engineer you will help build the development and deployment infrastructure used by our Space Communications team, which provides infrastructure for a wide variety of US Government satellites.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL BE FOCUSING ON&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting AWS-hosted and on-premises Kubernetes environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helping maintain reliable, secure, and highly available platform infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining and improving GitLab CI/CD pipelines to support software delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing and maintaining Infrastructure as Code using Terraform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assisting with Kubernetes application deployments using Helm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshooting infrastructure, platform, and application issues across AWS and Kubernetes environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with software engineers to improve deployment automation and developer workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improving platform observability, automation, reliability, and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting software deployments into classified environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in Linux environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Python or Go through professional work, internships, coursework, or personal projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to Kubernetes, AWS, Terraform, or other cloud-native technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Git for source control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting and analytical problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to learn new technologies and adapt quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to obtain and maintain a U.S. government TS/SCI clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOU MIGHT BE A GOOD FIT IF&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy building and automating technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You like digging into complex technical problems and figuring out how things work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve built projects outside of the classroom or workplace because you’re curious and enjoy learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re comfortable collaborating with teammates and asking questions when you need help.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take ownership of your work and are eager to continuously improve your technical skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re excited to work on mission-critical software that supports national security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;LOCATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is a hybrid role based in Colorado Springs, CO that offers flexibility while supporting collaboration on classified work. This role will require onsite work as needed to support secure program requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is between $75,000 and $112,000 base salary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BENEFITS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compensation includes competitive salary, meaningful equity ownership, profit sharing, employer 401(k) contribution, and 100% employer covered medical, dental, and vision insurance for you and your dependents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ELIGIBILITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must be a US Citizen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must be able to obtain and hold a U.S. TS/SCI security clearance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO STATEMENT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;At Sphinx Defense, we are devoted to building a team that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills. Sphinx Defense is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, and gender identity.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLEARANCE ELIGIBILITY - This position requires eligibility to obtain and maintain a U.S. security clearance. &lt;/strong&gt;For more information about U.S. Security Clearances:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;postings-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.state.gov/security-clearances#:~:text=Security%20clearances%20only%20apply%20to,behalf%20of%20the%20federal%20government.&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful, permanent resident (aka green card holder), (iii) Refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) Asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, or be eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State. Learn more about the ITAR&amp;nbsp;&lt;a class=&quot;postings-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.pmddtc.state.gov/?id=ddtc_kb_article_page&amp;amp;sys_id=24d528fddbfc930044f9ff621f961987&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT SPHINX&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sphinx builds software to solve complex national security problems in Space. Founded by engineers and technologists with deep experience across commercial and defense technology, we were frustrated by the outdated and insecure technology America&#39;s service members are forced to rely on. We&#39;re here to do better.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re focused on building modern, scalable products with an emphasis on using open source technologies. Expect talented, motivated, and interesting colleagues who emphasize collaboration, transparency, and individual responsibility.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sphinx is hiring a Backend Engineer to join our Space Communications team building a ground communications and data-transport&amp;nbsp; platform for US government satellites. As a Backend Engineer you will lead the development of core platform services, designing and&amp;nbsp; building technology to support the operations of a wide variety of US&amp;nbsp; Government satellites. You&#39;ll work as both an individual contributor and a lead for more junior engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for a track record of the following:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on&amp;nbsp; multi-tenant services on public cloud platforms like AWS, Azure, or GCP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing and consuming APIs and services as part of platform ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing with an emphasis on automation and security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to own a technical problem end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A habit of self-directed learning of new technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work well with a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to communicate clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You might be a good fit if:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 3-5+ years’ of progressively responsible software engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have extensive experience with Python, FastAPI, postgres, AWS, Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience architecting and building APIs and backend services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can demonstrate in-depth knowledge of at least one commercial cloud platform and its associated services&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable working with some ambiguity and able to self-direct your work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve made enough mistakes and booked enough wins to know what not to build and know what good looks like&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience working in space, satellite communications, or building ground systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LOCATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While this role is remote, the potential for travel may occur such as client visits, company gatherings, and other project related travel as needed may be required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role is between $138,000 - $167,000 base salary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quarterly bonus structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity ownership in the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% Premium coverage for medical, dental, and vision for you and dependents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Savings Accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401k employer contribution plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible paid time off policy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible work/remote work policy&lt;/li&gt;
